    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-184782",
      "sequence_position": 7,
      "problem": "Let $n$ be an integer. Using the contrapositive, prove that $3n+8$ is odd implies $n$ is odd.\n\nThe contrapositive form of the given statement is as follows:\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}\\,⇒\\,{{field-2}}\n$$\n\nWe'll prove this statement instead of the original one.\n\nIf $n$ is {{field-3}}, then $n=$ {{field-4}} for some integer $a.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3n+8 & ={{field-5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $b=$ {{field-6}}. Since $a$ is {{field-7}}, we have that $b$ is {{field-8}}.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3n+8 & ={{field-9}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich {{field-10}} a multiple of $2.$ Hence, $3n+8$ is {{field-11}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Recall the following:\n\n- If an integer $n$ is even, then there exists an integer $p$ such that $n=2p.$\n\n- If an integer $n$ is odd, then there exists an integer $q$ such that $n=2q+1.$\n\nIn this case, we need to prove the following:\n\n$$\n3n+8\\text{ is odd}\\,⇒\\,n\\text{ is odd}\n$$\n\nTo prove $P⇒Q,$ it suffices to prove the contrapositive $¬Q⇒¬P.$ So, let's write down the contrapositive of our statement.\n\nThe contrapositive form of the given statement is as follows:\n\n$$\nn\\text{ is even}\\,⇒\\,3n+8\\text{ is even}\n$$\n\nWe'll prove this statement instead of the original one.\n\nWe start by using the fact that $n$ is even.\n\nIf $n$ is even, then $n=2a$ for some integer $a.$\n\nThe idea is to substitute $n=2a$ into the expression $3n+8$ and show it is even by writing it as a multiple of  $2$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3n+8 & =3(2a)+8 \\\\  & =6a+8 \\\\  & =2{{(3a+4)}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we define another integer $b=3a+4$ (highlighted above), we have that $3n+8=2b,$ which shows that $3n+8$ is indeed  a multiple of $2.$\n\nLet $b=3a+4.$ Since $a$ is an integer, we have that $b$ is an integer.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3n+8 & =2{{(3a+4)}_{⏟}}_{b} \\\\  & =2b,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a multiple of $2.$\n\nFinally, we write our conclusion.\n\nTherefore, $3n+8$ is even.",
